          "tier": 2,
          "publisher": "National Gallery"
        }
      }
    ],
    "moment": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "Dutch maritime painting was an important precedent for Turner, and he may have been stimulated to paint Calais Pier when, towards the end of his trip, he saw (and sketched) Jacob van Ruisdael’s A Storm at Sea off the Dykes of Holland (1670) in the Louvre.",
        "source": {
          "author": "National Gallery",
          "title": "Calais Pier",
          "readAt": "https://www.nationalgallery.org.uk/paintings/joseph-mallord-william-turner-calais-pier",
